  "reply_construction_scope": [
    "Logical replies are freshly constructed codec inputs, not daemon-produced replies or proof of execution, staging, durability, header storage, caps, ENOENT semantics or server limits.",
    "The public MOSDOpReply constructor keeps the request READ/WRITE/RETURNVEC mode bits and replaces only ONDISK/ONNVRAM/ACK with the explicit acktype: ONDISK for all-success and failok-clear, ACK for header-empty and none for rmkeys-enoent.",
    "Public claim_ops supplies input-union echoes and explicit outdata/results. Native merge_osd_op_vector_out_data independently derives payload_len and vector output order.",
    "The all-success reply carries raw GETHEADER bytes 00ff480a80 without a length prefix and four mutation results 0 without output.",
    "header-empty is a single GETHEADER result 0 with empty output; rmkeys-enoent is a single RMKEYS{6b} with aggregate and per-op -2; failok-clear is CLEAR(FAILOK) per-op -2 followed by SETVALS{6b->76} result 0 with aggregate 0."
  ],
